// THE BOUND ON D207's RUNG, AS A PROGRAM — the `-3` map-value floor with NO destination.
// Must keep LOUD-REJECTING (`emitProgram: unsupported map value type`).
//
// Delete the `type Circle` line and this runs: `structIndexOfObjCtx` adopts the literal onto
// Circle's row through `anonValueFitsField`'s union-box leniency, which also SUPPRESSES the
// `#anon` row `collectAnonShapes` would have minted, and the mv layer then asks under a
// render that names nothing. That is **D461** — D207 closes only the half with a destination.
// (D207's row cited this as "filed as D209". It was not: D209 closed 2026-08-28 and its own
// repro is the LIST spelling. The map spelling had no row until D461.)
//
// WHY THIS CELL EARNS ITS PLACE. D207's rung is a FIND: `letMapDestShape` interns nothing, so
// it can only make a binding land on a slot that already EXISTS. Measured with a `tErr` probe
// on the closing compiler, this program REACHES the rung (`reach=1`) and gets no answer
// (`ans=0`) — the destination scan finds none. The day someone makes that rung MINT instead
// of find, this cell starts running and the FIND discipline (D-MAPNODETY's rule, the one that
// keeps 128 measured slot moves off the table) has been dropped without anyone saying so.
// A `runs` cell cannot express that; only a cell that must stay refused can.
type Circle = { r: i32 | null }
const lv1 = Map()
lv1["k0"] = { r: 7 }
print(lv1.size)
